\section{print()}{

Every printout follows the style shared with nomologR (see
\link{contentvalidR-package}): a header naming the object's class and what it
holds, then the facts of the design, then the verdict, then tables with
numbers in APA style and, for most results, a key to the columns and
decisions shown. A printout ends with a line pointing to what else the
object holds. Only the display is rounded: the object keeps every value at
full precision. \code{print()} returns its argument invisibly.

Most methods take \code{digits}, the decimal places for estimates; \emph{p} values
always get three. The item-sort and expert-panel printouts also take
\code{legacy}, which shows the earlier published rules beside the decision
without changing it, and the glossary takes \code{width}.
\code{options(contentvalidR.show_key = FALSE)} hides the keys.

What each kind of result prints:
\itemize{
\item \strong{Workflow fits} from \code{\link[=sort_validity]{sort_validity()}}, \code{\link[=rating_validity]{rating_validity()}},
\code{\link[=expert_validity]{expert_validity()}}, \code{\link[=delphi_validity]{delphi_validity()}}, \code{\link[=judge_validity]{judge_validity()}}, and
\code{\link[=domain_validity]{domain_validity()}}: the full evidence, one row per unit of analysis,
with the scale- or panel-level evidence and what the evidence does not
decide.
\item \strong{Component indices} from \code{\link[=compute_psa]{compute_psa()}}, \code{\link[=compute_csv]{compute_csv()}}, \code{\link[=htc]{htc()}},
\code{\link[=htd]{htd()}}, \code{\link[=anova_content]{anova_content()}}, \code{\link[=aikens_v]{aikens_v()}}, \code{\link[=cvr]{cvr()}}, \code{\link[=ioc]{ioc()}}, \code{\link[=cvi]{cvi()}},
\code{\link[=panel_agreement]{panel_agreement()}}, \code{\link[=csv_binom_test]{csv_binom_test()}}, \code{\link[=interpret_colquitt]{interpret_colquitt()}},
\code{\link[=colquitt_benchmarks]{colquitt_benchmarks()}}, and \code{\link[=similarity_from_sort]{similarity_from_sort()}}: the index as a
formatted table or a short report. Apart from printing, these results
behave as the plain data frame, list, or matrix they hold.
\item \strong{Planning and diagnostics} from \code{\link[=sort_power]{sort_power()}}, \code{\link[=expert_power]{expert_power()}},
